 "toneLesson": {
  "title": "Vowels, initials and casual sounds",
  "card": {
   "title": "How people really say it",
   "explain": "Many Hongkongers, especially family at home, change a few sounds: n- becomes l- (你 (nei5) sounds like 'lei5'), ng- is dropped (我 (ngo5) sounds like 'o5'), gw- becomes g- (廣 (gwong2) sounds like 'gong2'). Some words also take a changed tone in speech: 名 (meng2), 錢 (cin2). Understand both; say whichever feels natural.",
